# sedai_group_settings (Resource)

Manages the top-level settings for a Sedai group. The provider auto-initializes the group's settings on first apply, so the customer never has to call the init API directly. Only attributes specified in this resource are tracked for drift — unmanaged per-resource-type tuning (kube scaling, etc.) is preserved as-is.

## Example Usage: aggression mode (Turbo)

`aggression_mode` sets how aggressively Sedai optimizes Kubernetes and ECS workloads: `PROD`, `EXPEDITE` or `TURBO` ("Speed" in the Sedai UI, Kubernetes only). It is not `optimization_mode`. It needs Sedai 1.148 or later and an admin-role API key.

